<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Maria Vladimirovna Staritskaya</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1560">1560</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Maria Staritskaya</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Maria Vladimirovna Staritskaya was a Russian princess, daughter of Prince Vladimir of Staritsa and a relative of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tsar">Tsar</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-iv-of-russia">Ivan IV</a>. In 1573 she married Duke Magnus of Holstein, whom Ivan had made king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonia">Livonia</a> as his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a>. After Magnus died in 1583 she lived in Riga, then returned to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, where she was made to become a nun.</p></div>
